\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Empirical Lipschitz constants of the PRISM bound (Theorem~\ref {thm:unified_bound}) for each evaluated model. $K_{\mathrm  {pred}} = \sqrt  {2}$ holds universally (Appendix~\ref {app:head_bound}, simplex polarization), independent of model. $K_{\mathrm  {feat}}$ is empirical per model, depending on the spread of token embeddings in $H_T$; for the 8B-scale models studied here, $K_{\mathrm  {feat}}$ ranges from $\approx 0.93$ (Mistral family) to $\approx 3.46$ (Qwen3-Base). Since $K_{\mathrm  {feat}}$ is a constant per model, it scales the bound's magnitude but does not affect the within-model rank correlation that PRISM is calibrated to.}}{16}{table.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:lipschitz_constants}{{4}{16}{Empirical Lipschitz constants of the PRISM bound (Theorem~\ref {thm:unified_bound}) for each evaluated model. $K_{\mathrm {pred}} = \sqrt {2}$ holds universally (Appendix~\ref {app:head_bound}, simplex polarization), independent of model. $K_{\mathrm {feat}}$ is empirical per model, depending on the spread of token embeddings in $H_T$; for the 8B-scale models studied here, $K_{\mathrm {feat}}$ ranges from $\approx 0.93$ (Mistral family) to $\approx 3.46$ (Qwen3-Base). Since $K_{\mathrm {feat}}$ is a constant per model, it scales the bound's magnitude but does not affect the within-model rank correlation that PRISM is calibrated to}{table.4}{}}
